<style>
/* ── Ingredient Science Cards — self-contained ── */
.fg-sci { background:var(--fg-canvas); padding:80px 0; }
.fg-sci__inner { max-width:var(--container-max); margin:0 auto; padding:0 var(--container-pad); }
.fg-sci__overline { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; font-family:var(--font-body); font-size:var(--fs-label); font-weight:600; letter-spacing:var(--track-label); text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--fg-orange); margin-bottom:20px; }
.fg-sci__overline::before { content:''; display:block; width:24px; height:2px; background:currentColor; border-radius:1px; flex-shrink:0; }
.fg-sci__headline { font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:clamp(28px,3.2vw,48px); font-weight:800; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:var(--track-display); line-height:1.05; color:var(--fg-ink); margin:0 0 56px; }
.fg-sci__cards { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:28px; }
.fg-sci-card { display:grid; grid-template-columns:320px 1fr; gap:0; align-items:stretch; background:#fff; border-radius:var(--radius-lg); overflow:hidden; border:1px solid var(--fg-border); box-shadow:0 4px 24px rgba(24,6,26,.06); }
.fg-sci-card--flip { grid-template-columns:1fr 320px; }
.fg-sci-card__img { width:100%; height:100%; min-height:240px; object-fit:cover; display:block; }
.fg-sci-card--flip .fg-sci-card__img { order:2; }
.fg-sci-card--flip .fg-sci-card__body { order:1; }
.fg-sci-card__body { padding:36px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:center; }
.fg-sci-card__label { font-family:var(--font-body); font-size:10px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--fg-orange); margin-bottom:10px; }
.fg-sci-card__title { font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:clamp(20px,2.4vw,28px); font-weight:800; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--fg-ink); margin:0 0 14px; line-height:1.1; }
.fg-sci-card__copy { font-family:var(--font-body); font-size:15px; font-weight:300; color:var(--fg-muted); line-height:1.7; margin:0; }
.fg-sci__disclaimer { font-family:var(--font-body); font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-muted); margin-top:28px; line-height:1.6; }
@media(max-width:900px) {
  .fg-sci-card, .fg-sci-card--flip { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
  .fg-sci-card--flip .fg-sci-card__img, .fg-sci-card--flip .fg-sci-card__body { order:unset; }
  .fg-sci-card__img { min-height:200px; }
  .fg-sci-card__body { padding:24px; }
}
</style>

<section class="fg-sci" id="fg-science">
  <div class="fg-sci__inner">
    <p class="fg-sci__overline" data-aos="fade-up">The Science Behind It</p>
    <h2 class="fg-sci__headline" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="60">Every Ingredient Has a Job</h2>

    <div class="fg-sci__cards">

      <div class="fg-sci-card" data-aos="fade-up">
        <img class="fg-sci-card__img"
             src="{{ 'fg-fiber-impacts.webp' | asset_url }}"
             alt="Prebiotic fiber — gut health support"
             loading="lazy">
        <div class="fg-sci-card__body">
          <div class="fg-sci-card__label">Prebiotic Fiber</div>
          <h3 class="fg-sci-card__title">Feed the Good Bacteria</h3>
          <p class="fg-sci-card__copy">Fructooligosaccharides (FOS) are plant-derived prebiotic fibers that selectively feed Lactobacillus and Bifidobacterium &mdash; the beneficial bacteria in your gut. When these bacteria thrive, they produce short-chain fatty acids that may support gut lining integrity, help reduce inflammation, and support healthy digestion. FlushGut delivers 7.5g per serving &mdash; the equivalent of 15 standard fiber capsules.*</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="fg-sci-card fg-sci-card--flip" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="60">
        <img class="fg-sci-card__img"
             src="{{ 'fg-orange-box.png' | asset_url }}"
             alt="Probiotic strains — microbiome support"
             loading="lazy">
        <div class="fg-sci-card__body">
          <div class="fg-sci-card__label">510M CFU Probiotic</div>
          <h3 class="fg-sci-card__title">Rebuild Your Microbiome</h3>
          <p class="fg-sci-card__copy">FlushGut&rsquo;s probiotic strains are delivered in a jelly matrix that supports their stability through your digestive tract &mdash; unlike capsules that often degrade before reaching your gut. 510 million colony-forming units per serving, with clinically studied strains designed to support microbiome diversity and digestive regularity.*</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="fg-sci-card" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="120">
        <img class="fg-sci-card__img"
             src="{{ 'fg-box-scene.webp' | asset_url }}"
             alt="FlushGut jelly format — smooth and flavorful"
             loading="lazy">
        <div class="fg-sci-card__body">
          <div class="fg-sci-card__label">Jelly Format</div>
          <h3 class="fg-sci-card__title">Why Jelly Works Better</h3>
          <p class="fg-sci-card__copy">Pills dissolve inconsistently. Powders require mixing and often taste bad. Gummies are loaded with sugar. FlushGut&rsquo;s jelly format means the active ingredients are already in solution &mdash; supporting faster uptake and smoother delivery. Smooth texture. Real Berry or Orange flavor. No aftertaste. Just tear, squeeze, and support your gut 3 times a week.*</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <p class="fg-sci__disclaimer">*These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Ingredient Science Cards",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "fg-sci",
  "presets": [{ "name": "Ingredient Science Cards" }]
}
{% endschema %}
